      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The 1823 Manzano Land Grant brought roughly 160 families from the Rio Grande Valley, establishing the community’s ranching roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/manzano_springs_new_mexico",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During the Great Depression, the Civilian Conservation Corps built Camp SCS‑21 near Mountainair, creating trails and picnic areas that still welcome visitors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
